Jesssica wrote:
> Is it better to delve as deep into the dungeon as possible, going
> downstairs whenever you find a staircase, or to explore every level
> before going down further?

Here's my general game strategy:


When you are low level it is a good idea to explore every level to find
more items.  Finding certain items, like boots of speed or gauntlets of
power, can make life a lot easier in the beginning.

Usually I reach a point where I am fairly well armed and have some nice
gear.  Once I've done the Mines and Sobokan I descend as quickly as
possible to find Medusa's level.  This way I know how big the dungeon
section is.  Then I go back up and map out each level, looking for
vaults, Ludios, the quest, altars, temples, and so on.  Once I've got
the whole Dungeon section mapped out I kill Medusa and do the Castle,
using the wishes to flesh out my kit.  Whether or not I do Ludios and
the Quest before or after this depends on the class I'm playing.

Then I enchant up my armor and weapons, alchemize potions, and head
into Hell.  In Hell my goals are to kill the 4 guaranteed demon
princes, find and clear Vlad's Tower (guaranteed AoLS and WW boots),
find and clear the Wizard's tower, and find the vibrating square.

Before I go on the ascension run I make sure my stuff is is highly
enchanted, I have at least 300 hp, my important spells are refreshed,
and that I have the important items for Astral.  Then I grab the BotD,
do the Sanctum and run back up.  Run through Elemental Planes and go
through Astral.



